## Files this task touched that another task owns

- native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/render/{mod,painter,text,images}.rs (render-core, finished): the paint stage is the extension
  of `Painter` the render-core result named; the operators are routed to the new files, `show_text` returns a `Result`, the
  pattern branches of fill, stroke, text and image masks call `pattern.rs`.
- native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/oplist/mod.rs and interpreter.rs (oplist, finished): `oplist::get_page_operators` returns the
  operator list with the fonts the evaluator loaded (`PageOperators`), `Evaluator::into_fonts` hands them over; `get_operator_list`
  is unchanged for its callers. `render_page` uses it so the glyph procedures of Type3 fonts reach the painter. A list built by the
  caller and painted with `render_operator_list` does not bring its fonts: its Type3 text moves the text position and draws nothing.

## What the rasteriser still needs from other tasks

- nr-office-pdf-render-pages (mixdog-office-pdf) calls `render::render_page`; its `RenderOptions` literal is unchanged.
- The font bridge (a `FontProvider` and a `FontDrawing` that turns a font program into outlines) is still nobody's in the tree:
  without it text is not drawn and the Type3 glyph procedures are only exercised by the unit tests.

No service, protocol method or SERVICE_PENDING name comes from this task.
